accel/tcg: keep jump-cache entries that a TLB change does not touch.

Measured on the vphone during Home-screen swipes (six vCPUs, 16 KiB target
pages): 6.9 million jump-cache misses a second went to the TB hash table,
about a fifth of TCG time with the lookup helpers. Two kinds of flush
caused nearly all of them.

A page flush (TLBI by address or range, ~50,000 a second) cleared its page's
whole jump-cache partition and the one of the page before: 2 x 2048 entries,
with every other page that hashed there. It now clears only entries of TBs
that start on the page, or start on the page before and run into it, and
visits only occupied entries (a bitmap the owner keeps); the page before is
looked at only when its partition ever held a TB that crosses a page.

An ASID change (TTBR0/1_EL1 with a new ASID, ~5,000 a second; iOS changes it
on every context switch) flushed the whole jump cache with the TLB. A stage 1
descriptor with nG clear in a regime with two VA ranges is the same for every
ASID, so the walk now records that in CPUTLBEntryFull.asid_global (false
everywhere else; a two-stage translation keeps stage 1's answer). A fill marks
its entry global when the TLB holds the TB's code pages that way, and the new
tlb_flush_asid_change clears the TLB as before but of the jump cache only the
entries filled from non-global code, from their own log, or through the
bitmap once that overflows. A full flush that overflowed its fill log walks
the bitmap too instead of storing to all 65536 entries. The entries stay 16
bytes for the translated-code probes.

On the vphone the misses fell to 3.8 million a second. Against the same series
without this patch, the engine's CPU time over tools/ios_measure.py's workload
went from 475 to 433 s; launch, tap and swipe medians (of five) moved less
than their spread (swipe 10.0 -> 11.5 changed frames per second).

tests/engine/jump-cache-probe.S now maps its alias window non-global: its
asid phase changed a global mapping without a TLBI, which the architecture
does not require to take effect.

